msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1707
msgid "Selects how quickly the automatic gain control lets the receiver recover after a strong signal. Fast suits CW and data, Slow suits SSB and AM, and Auto picks Slow for SSB and AM and Fast for the other modes. With AGC off the S-meter no longer moves and strong signals are likely to distort."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1819
msgid "Selects one of ten DSP equalizer curves for your transmitted voice. 0 is flat, 1 to 3 reduce the low, middle or high frequencies, and 4 to 6 boost the high, middle or low frequencies. 7 boosts the lows and reduces the highs, 8 reduces the lows and boosts the middle, and 9 reduces the lows and boosts the highs."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1475
msgid "Selects the characters the CW training feature sends: digits only, letters only, or both mixed. Training plays random five character Morse groups through the sidetone at the CW speed, without transmitting."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:949
msgid "Selects the data mode a DIG channel uses. RTTY is FSK radioteletype keyed by a terminal unit or RTTY software, while USER-L and USER-U carry audio based data modes such as packet on the lower or upper sideband. N/A is for channels that are not in DIG mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:2007
msgid "Selects the language for spoken radio-operation prompts, or disables those prompts."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:722
msgid "Selects the language of the menus and the spoken voice prompts."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1793
msgid "Selects the mark tone for RTTY: 2125 Hz for high tone operation or 1275 Hz for low tone operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1757
msgid "Selects the memory channel that F+9 jumps to, so that an important channel can be reached with one key press."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:2686
msgid "Selects the special DTMF digit interpreted as a group-call wildcard by the decoder. Off assigns no group-call digit."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:2678
msgid "Selects the special DTMF digit interpreted as a separator by the decoder."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1008
msgid "Selects the squelch-tail elimination setting used for communication through a compatible repeater. Use 0 ms when the repeater does not support this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:822
msgid "Selects the tone-burst frequency sent for repeater access."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1606
msgid "Selects what the LOCK button locks. Frequencies locks the controls that change the frequency, including the microphone UP, DWN and FAST keys. Panel locks all front panel keys and knobs, and All locks both the front panel and the microphone keys. POWER and LOCK always remain usable."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1373
msgid "Selects what the TUNE button controls. ATAS is the optional ATAS-100/-120 active-tuning antenna, EXT ATU the optional FC-40 external tuner, and INT ATU the built-in tuner acting on the transmit signal only, while INTRATU puts the built-in tuner in the receive path as well. F-TRANS instead sends this radio's frequency to a second radio of the same model whenever TUNE is pressed, for single operator two radio (SO2R) operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1738
msgid "Selects what the meter shows while transmitting: PO the average power output, ALC the relative ALC voltage, or SWR the standing wave ratio of the antenna. While receiving it always shows the signal strength."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1611
msgid "Selects whether the radio uses DTMF codes, together with CTCSS or DCS, to decide when to unmute the speaker on this channel. Off unmutes it on the correct CTCSS or DCS alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1257
#, python-format
msgid "Selects which of the %i programmed DTMF PTT-ID codes VFO A uses. Edit the code itself under DTMF Encode Settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1269
#, python-format
msgid "Selects which of the %i programmed DTMF PTT-ID codes VFO B uses. Edit the code itself under DTMF Encode Settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1585
#, python-format
msgid "Selects which of the %i programmed DTMF PTT-ID codes this channel transmits. Edit the code itself under DTMF Encode Settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1055
msgid "Selects which of the eleven noise reduction algorithms is used. Each one is designed for a different kind of noise, so try them in turn to find the one that best suppresses the noise currently heard. Off also turns DSP Noise Reduction off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:958
msgid "Selects which of the two scan lists include this channel. Channel scanning steps through the channels of the scan list chosen with Default scanlist."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1692
msgid "Selects which scan list channel scanning steps through. Add a channel to a list with its Scanlists setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1233
msgid "Selects wide or narrow FM for VFO A. Use Narrow where required by the channel plan to reduce interference to adjacent channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1245
msgid "Selects wide or narrow FM for VFO B. Use Narrow where required by the channel plan to reduce interference to adjacent channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:769 ../drivers/uvk5.py:2046
msgid "Sends a short tone at the end of each transmission so other stations can hear that you released PTT."
msgstr ""

#: ../wxui/query_sources.py:357
msgid "Service"
msgstr "服务"

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1150
msgid "Sets VFO A's repeater shift direction. + transmits above the receive frequency, - transmits below it, and Off uses the same frequency for transmit and receive."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1163
msgid "Sets VFO B's repeater shift direction. + transmits above the receive frequency, - transmits below it, and Off uses the same frequency for transmit and receive."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1281
msgid "Sets how far VFO A moves for each tuning step and while scanning in Frequency mode. Choose the spacing used by the frequencies you intend to tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1294
msgid "Sets how far VFO B moves for each tuning step and while scanning in Frequency mode. Choose the spacing used by the frequencies you intend to tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1631
msgid "Sets how far the frequency moves for each step of the MAIN DIAL knob: 1, 10 or 20 Hz in SSB and CW, 100 or 200 Hz in AM and FM."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1640
msgid "Sets how long a button has to be held to activate its press and hold function. A shorter press activates the button's normal function."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:620 ../drivers/uvk5.py:1524
msgid "Sets how long each DTMF tone is transmitted. Increase this if the receiving system does not reliably decode the digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1512
msgid "Sets how long the * and # DTMF tones are transmitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:654
msgid "Sets how long the DTMF decoder remains active after a valid code before returning to its normal state."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1501
msgid "Sets how long the first DTMF tone of each code is transmitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:882
msgid "Sets how long the menu stays open without a key press before the radio leaves it."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1398
msgid "Sets how long the transmitter stays on after you stop sending in semi break-in CW, in steps of 10 ms, so 25 means 250 ms. A longer delay suits operators who pause often while sending. The radio can also be set to FULL, full break-in, which lets you hear between the characters you send."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1750
msgid "Sets how long the transmitter stays on after you stop speaking in VOX operation, in steps of 100 ms, so 5 means 500 ms. A longer delay keeps short pauses in your speech from switching the radio back to receive."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1488
msgid "Sets how many milliseconds the radio transmits before it sends the first DTMF tone, so that the receiving radio has time to unmute. The radio's menu offers 30 to 990 ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:741
msgid "Sets how many seconds the display backlight remains on after a key press or radio activity."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1912
msgid "Sets how many seconds the display backlight stays on before it turns off by itself. Off keeps the backlight turned off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1475
msgid "Sets how many seconds the radio lets you talk with the caller after it decodes a DTMF call to its ID. After that time, a new DTMF call is needed. The factory setting is 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:666 ../drivers/uvk5.py:1768
msgid "Sets how strong a received signal must be before the speaker unmutes. 0 leaves the squelch open so you hear noise all the time, higher values reject more weak signals and noise. Raise this value if the speaker keeps unmuting on interference, lower it if distant stations are being cut off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:995
msgid "Sets how strongly the contour filter boosts or cuts. Low gives a gentle effect, High a stronger one."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:2069
#, python-format
msgid "Sets line %d of the welcome text that the radio shows at power-on when Power on display mode is Welcome Info."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1677
#, python-format
msgid "Sets priority channel 1 of scan list %d. With priority scanning on, the radio checks it before each regular channel it scans. 0 means no priority channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1681
#, python-format
msgid "Sets priority channel 2 of scan list %d. With priority scanning on, the radio checks it after priority channel 1, before each regular channel it scans. 0 means no priority channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1648
msgid "Sets the 3-character DTMF ID of this contact, using 0-9, A-D, * and #. Leave it empty for an unused entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1622
msgid "Sets the 5-character DTMF code that disables this radio when another radio sends it, if Permit remote kill is on."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1641
msgid "Sets the 5-character DTMF code that enables this radio again after the kill code has disabled it."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1467
msgid "Sets the CW sidetone volume, from 0 to 100, used when CW sidetone volume Linked is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1586
msgid "Sets the DTMF code that the radio sends when PTT is pressed, on channels whose PTTID setting sends the up code."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1603
msgid "Sets the DTMF code that the radio sends when PTT is released, on channels whose PTTID setting sends the down code."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1768
msgid "Sets the VOX sensitivity used in DIG mode, so that the audio from the data equipment switches the transmitter on without a PTT line. 0 turns VOX off in DIG mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1041 ../drivers/uvk5.py:1819
msgid "Sets the VOX sensitivity. Too sensitive a setting keys the transmitter on the noise around the radio, too insensitive a setting fails to pick up your voice."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1759
msgid "Sets the VOX sensitivity. Too sensitive a setting keys the transmitter on the noise around the radio, too insensitive a setting fails to pick up your voice. 1 is the least sensitive setting and 100 the most."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1304
msgid "Sets the baud rate of the CAT jack, which must match the computer control software. Data turns the CAT jack into an RTTY interface instead: RTTY software keys the FSK shift through the serial data input and uses RTS as PTT."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1565
msgid "Sets the beep volume relative to the receive audio level set by AF GAIN, when Beep volume Linked is on. 0 makes the beep as loud as the received audio, negative values make it quieter and positive values louder."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1574
msgid "Sets the beep volume, from 0 to 100, used when Beep volume Linked is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1587
msgid "Sets the brightness of the display illumination, from 1 to 8."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:592
#, python-format
msgid "Sets the call name for DTMF code %i, up to 10 characters long."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1438
msgid "Sets the character that separates the called ID from this radio's own ID in a DTMF call. With *, radio 100 calls radio 123 by sending 123*100."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1449
msgid "Sets the character that stands for any digit in a called DTMF ID, so that one call reaches a group of radios. With #, sending 12# calls the radios with IDs 120 to 129, 1## calls IDs 100 to 199, and ### calls all radios."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1580
msgid "Sets the contrast of the display, from 1 to 24. Changing it here has not been seen to have a visible effect on the radio."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:873
msgid "Sets the current keypad-lock state."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1968
msgid "Sets the current keypad-lock state. Hold the # key on the radio to lock or unlock the keypad."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1017
msgid "Sets the delay before repeater squelch-tail elimination is applied. Match this timing to the repeater; use 0 ms when the feature is not required."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1439
msgid "Sets the delay between closing the key and the carrier being transmitted in QSK operation with the built-in keyer. At 25 ms keep the CW speed at 50 wpm or below, and at 30 ms at 42 wpm or below, or the radio cannot transmit."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1186
msgid "Sets the difference in MHz between VFO A's receive and transmit frequencies. The Shift setting determines whether this offset is added or subtracted."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1197
msgid "Sets the difference in MHz between VFO B's receive and transmit frequencies. The Shift setting determines whether this offset is added or subtracted."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1430
msgid "Sets the dot to dash ratio of the built-in electronic keyer. At 1:3.0, the standard weighting, a dash lasts three times as long as a dot."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:2086
msgid "Sets the frequency of this broadcast FM radio preset, in MHz from 76 to 108. Leave it empty to clear the preset."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1785
msgid "Sets the frequency shift between the mark and space tones in FSK RTTY. Most amateur RTTY uses 170 Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1831
msgid "Sets the microphone gain for SSB, AM and FM. Use Low with a microphone that has a high output, Normal with the supplied hand microphone and High with a microphone that has a low output. The speech processor is off at Low and on at the other settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1834
msgid "Sets the microphone sensitivity, from 0 to 4. Raise it if other stations hear you too quietly, lower it if your audio sounds distorted."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1645
msgid "Sets the name of this entry in the DTMF contact list. The radio's D-LIST menu shows the list, so that you can pick a contact and call it directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1346
msgid "Sets the offset Quick Split applies. Holding SPLIT/STEP for a second sets the transmit VFO to the receive frequency plus this offset, in the same mode as the receive VFO, and turns split operation on."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1502
msgid "Sets the pause in seconds between repeats of a CW beacon message. 0 turns the repeat off, so that each message is sent once per button press, as with a CW message keyer."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1410
msgid "Sets the pitch of the CW sidetone, which is also the offset of the transmitted carrier and the center of the CW receive filter. Tuning a station in until its tone matches the sidetone puts you on its frequency."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1551
msgid "Sets the pitch of the beep the radio sounds to confirm button presses."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1130
msgid "Sets the receive frequency shown on display line A in Frequency (VFO) mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:1139
msgid "Sets the receive frequency shown on display line B in Frequency (VFO) mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1418
msgid "Sets the sending speed of the built-in electronic keyer in words per minute. The radio can also show it in characters per minute, five times the wpm value. With a CW QSK delay of 25 ms keep it at 50 wpm or below, and with 30 ms at 42 wpm or below, or the radio cannot transmit."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1457
msgid "Sets the sidetone volume relative to the receive audio level set by AF GAIN, when CW sidetone volume Linked is on. 0 makes the sidetone as loud as the received audio, negative values make it quieter and positive values louder."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/baofeng_uv17Pro.py:632 ../drivers/uvk5.py:1539
msgid "Sets the silent gap between transmitted DTMF tones. Increase this if the receiving system cannot separate adjacent digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1294
msgid "Sets the time-out timer for computer control commands arriving on the CAT jack. Command input that continues for longer than this time is cut off. The radio shows the shortest setting as 10 ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1386
msgid "Sets the transmit power in watts. Use the lowest power that provides reliable communication, and a half to a third of full power for data transmissions longer than a few minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1033
msgid "Sets the width of the DSP IF filter. A narrower filter rejects interference close to the signal, a wider one sounds more natural when the band is quiet. The widths depend on the mode: 1.8, 2.4 or 3.0 kHz for SSB, 300 Hz, 500 Hz or 2.4 kHz for CW, 300 Hz, 2.4 or 3.0 kHz for DIG, 3.0, 6.0 or 9.0 kHz for AM, and 2.5 or 5.0 kHz for FM. A width the mode does not offer is replaced with the closest one it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:1568
msgid "Sets this radio's own 3-character DTMF ID. The radio sends it with its DTMF calls, and other radios call this radio with it. The radio's menu calls it ANI-ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/ft450d.py:1320
msgid "Sets when the scan resumes after it has paused on a signal. 1 to 10 resumes after that many seconds, 0 selects BUSY, which waits until the signal has gone. In SSB, CW and SSB based data modes the scanner instead steps slowly across a signal, giving you time to stop it."
msgstr ""

